# BASELINE\
baseline/single_prompt.py: ONE prompt to the same model with the catalogue pasted in and\
"Write a proposal for this enquiry." No pipeline, no checks.\
Run it on all tests BEFORE tuning the prototype prompts, and save the raw outputs.\
\
# EVALUATION\
eval/run_tests.py runs both the baseline and the prototype on every test and writes\
eval/results.csv plus eval/results.md (a markdown table).\
Columns: test id, input summary, expected behaviour, baseline result, prototype result,\
pass/fail for each, notes.\
\
Scoring per test, automatic where possible:\
- status correct;\
- total exactly matches the oracle (for the baseline, parse its stated total);\
- zero constraint violations;\
- zero forbidden promises;\
- clarification asks for the decision-critical missing fields.\
\
Run each LLM test 3 times if time allows and report consistency.\
Also log latency per run and token usage, and compute cost from a price-per-token constant\
that I can edit.\
\
Summarise quality, time and cost honestly, and label every estimate.\
If the baseline does well on some cases, say so.\
\
# UI (app.py, Streamlit, kept minimal)\
1. Text box for the enquiry, plus a dropdown to load any test case.\
2. The extracted brief shown as an editable table, with the evidence quotes visible.\
3. A status banner computed by code: green/amber/blue/red, with the reasons.\
4. A \uc0\u9989 /\u10060  checklist per requirement, the itemised price table, the budget delta, and the assumptions list.\
5. The draft text, with a permanent "DRAFT \'96 requires salesperson approval \'96 availability unconfirmed" header.\
   If the status is INFEASIBLE, show the label "Not sendable as an offer".\
6. Guard warnings, shown visibly.\
